Project: Django. Upgrade: 3.2 -> 4.2. Release of these items: 4.1.
Source: Django 4.1 release notes.

Label every item:
- risk = the change could break an application or deployment, require migration work, or create operational risk for SOME user upgrading across this release (removed or renamed APIs/settings/flags, changed defaults, behavior changes, raised minimum versions of runtimes/databases/dependencies, data or schema migration, required config changes, deprecated-and-removed features).
- context = accurate and useful but needs no user action at this release: explicitly "no user action required", a deprecation that still works (warning only), a purely additive new feature or option, documentation pointers.
- noise = credits, install/download commands, pure bug fixes that cannot change correct behavior, marketing text, headings with no content.

Return one label per item_id with a one-sentence reason grounded in the item text.

Items (JSON lines):
{"item_id": "d235b709fae2", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The Django test runner now returns a non-zero error code for unexpected successes from tests marked with unittest.expectedFailure."}
{"item_id": "9ef19212796e", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "CsrfViewMiddleware no longer masks the CSRF cookie like it does the CSRF token in the DOM."}
{"item_id": "811c62acd013", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "CsrfViewMiddleware now uses request.META['CSRF_COOKIE'] for storing the unmasked CSRF secret rather than a masked version. This is an undocumented, private API."}
{"item_id": "d62049d23ad8", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The ModelAdmin.actions and inlines attributes now default to an empty tuple rather than an empty list to discourage unintended mutation."}
{"item_id": "10bcd8c3f75a", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The type=\"text/css\" attribute is no longer included in <link> tags for CSS form media."}
{"item_id": "a945c6845fc3", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "formset:added and formset:removed JavaScript events are now pure JavaScript events and don't depend on jQuery. See admin-javascript-inline-form-events for more details on the change."}
{"item_id": "347f78e7a2ef", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The exc_info argument of the undocumented django.utils.log.log_response() function is replaced by exception."}
{"item_id": "e943e5b8eb13", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The size argument of the undocumented django.views.static.was_modified_since() function is removed."}
{"item_id": "275590062314", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The admin log out UI now uses POST requests."}
{"item_id": "10c38e88021c", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The undocumented InlineAdminFormSet.non_form_errors property is replaced by the non_form_errors() method. This is consistent with BaseFormSet."}
{"item_id": "c837d4645ffd", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "As per above, the cached template loader is now enabled in development. You may specify OPTIONS['loaders'] to override this, if necessary."}
{"item_id": "e3897c3ce3f3", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The undocumented django.contrib.auth.views.SuccessURLAllowedHostsMixin mixin is replaced by RedirectURLMixin."}
{"item_id": "7c13ed5ddcac", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "BaseConstraint subclasses must implement validate method to allow those constraints to be used for validation."}
{"item_id": "ed9cb67b5fac", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The undocumented URLResolver._is_callback(), URLResolver._callback_strs, and URLPattern.lookup_str() are moved to django.contrib.admindocs.utils."}
{"item_id": "3a088cfe5903", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The Model.full_clean method now converts an exclude value to a set. It's also preferable to pass an exclude value as a set to the Model.clean_fields, Model.full_clean, Model.validate_unique, and Model.validate_constraints methods."}
{"item_id": "64797d029ea0", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The minimum supported version of asgiref is increased from 3.4.1 to 3.5.2."}
{"item_id": "c88a783f2f23", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "Combined expressions no longer use the error-prone behavior of guessing output_field when argument types match. As a consequence, resolving an output_field for database functions and combined expressions may now crash with mixed types. You will need to explicitly set the output_field in such cases."}
{"item_id": "bac31edda1c1", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The makemessages command no longer changes .po files when up to date. In older versions, POT-Creation-Date was always updated."}
{"item_id": "774669112334", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Features deprecated in 4.1 / Log out via GET", "text": "Logging out via GET requests to the built-in logout view is deprecated. Use POST requests instead. If you want to retain the user experience of an HTML link, you can use a form that is styled to appear as a link: <form id=\"logout-form\" method=\"post\" action=\"{% url 'admin:logout' %}\"> {% csrf_token %} <button type=\"submit\">{% translate \"Log out\" %}</button> </form> #logout-form { display: inline; } #logout-form button { background: none; border: none; cursor: pointer; padding: 0; text-decoration: underline; }"}
{"item_id": "e3287f68a4af", "section": "Django 4.1 release notes / Features deprecated in 4.1 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The context for sitemap index templates of a flat list of URLs is deprecated. Custom sitemap index templates should be updated for the adjusted context variables, expecting a list of objects with location and optional lastmod attributes."}
